# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore

# ── Go build & test artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compiled binaries and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test
# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
# Go workspace files
go.work
go.work.sum
# Dependency directory (we vendor nothing; uncomment to include)
# vendor/

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/bin/
# Stray loadgen binary from `go build ./tests/load`
/load

# ── Frontend console (web/console) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Source is tracked; the built bundle (internal/api/console_dist) is committed so
# `go build` embeds it without needing Node. Only the toolchain output is ignored.
node_modules/
web/console/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Secrets & local state (never commit) ─────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds real secrets; .env.example is the committed template.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# Key / certificate material
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
# Issued license files (internal/license, cmd/licensegen) — never a customer's
# license artifact in this repo, only the issuing tool and public verify key.
*.lic
# Hardware-lock grace-period state (internal/license/grace.go) — persisted next
# to a .lic file as "<license_path>.hwgrace"; contains a customer machine's
# hardware fingerprint. Low-sensitivity (not key material) but no reason to
# ever land in git — same reasoning as the *.lic rule above.
*.hwgrace
*.pfx
# Redis dump (local dev)
*.rdb
dump.rdb
# gosec output (build artifact — was committed once by mistake)
gosec_results.json

# ── Editor / IDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── OS junk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Misc scratch / patch leftovers ───────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# marketing site — captured leads (PII), never commit
web/pilot-requests.jsonl
web/v3/node_modules/
web/v3/dist/

# Raw exports from the sample-report generator (regenerate with generate.sh)
demo/sample-report/out/

# Raw exports from the false-positive assessment (regenerate with run.sh). These
# are responses from a live third-party API and are not ours to commit.
demo/fp-assessment/out/

# Local pentest stand (scripts/pentest-stand.sh): throwaway keys, logs and a
# PostgreSQL data directory. Never anything that should be committed.
.stand/
